.TH FL-GREET 1 "November 2026" "fldesktop 0.1.0" "fldesktop"
.SH NAME
fl-greet \- graphical greeter for greetd
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfl-greet\fR [\fB\-\-demo\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A login screen for greetd(1). Run it inside the cage kiosk compositor with
\fBfl-greet-session\fR, e.g. in \fI/etc/greetd/config.toml\fR:
command = "fl-greet-session" (it runs "cage \-s \-d \-\- fl-greet" with the
cursor theme of greeter.ini). Sessions are read from /usr/share/wayland-sessions.
.PP
\fI/etc/fldesktop/greeter.ini\fR (Settings > Login Screen edits it) holds
[Greeter] \fBBackground\fR (a world readable image), \fBMinUid\fR,
\fBHideUsers\fR (comma separated), \fBRememberUser\fR, \fBClock24\fR and
\fBShowPowerButtons\fR; [Appearance] \fBTheme\fR (light or dark),
\fBAccent\fR and \fBFontSize\fR; [General] \fBIconTheme\fR; and [Cursor]
\fBTheme\fR and \fBSize\fR. An example is installed as
\fI/usr/share/fldesktop/greeter.ini.example\fR.
.PP
An on-screen keyboard is built in. \fBKeyboard=button\fR (the default) adds a
Keyboard button that shows it, \fBalways\fR shows it from the start (for
touch-only devices) and \fBnever\fR removes the button.
\fBKeyboardLayout\fR selects its layout: \fBus\fR, \fBde\fR or \fBfr\fR.
.SH FINGERPRINTS
fl-greet answers greetd's PAM conversation: with \fBpam_fprintd\fR in greetd's
PAM setup (\fI/etc/pam.d/greetd\fR, e.g. \fBauth sufficient pam_fprintd.so\fR
before the password line) it shows "Place your finger on the reader" and logs
in with a finger; an empty password field is fine then. The polkit password
dialog (\fBfl-polkit-agent\fR(1)) shows the same messages for polkit's PAM
setup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-demo\fR
Run without greetd; any user logs in with the password "demo".
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfl-wm\fR(1), \fBfl-session\fR(1), \fBfl-panel\fR(1)
